<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">love taught me to lie (and life taught me to die)</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;But then Adora leaves and Catra shatters. Adora finds new friends and replaces her in the blink of an eye, and that betrayal stings the worst because it doesnâ€™t even take Adora a second thought to leave everything sheâ€™s ever known behind.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;To leave &lt;em&gt;her&lt;/em&gt; behind.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;But she survives, because thatâ€™s all she knows how to do. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;She claws her way out of deathâ€™s jaws more times than she can count, crawls back to the surface even when sheâ€™s the one throwing herself off the cliff, lets herself become the villain that Rebellion thinks she is because she doesnâ€™t know how to be anything else, loses herself to bitterness and anger and darkness because itâ€™s all she has left.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Leaving the Horde isnâ€™t an option when she has nowhere else to go, so she becomes sharper and meaner and harder until sheâ€™s nothing more than the cutting edge of the Hordeâ€™s blade.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Or: A Catra character study.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>echoes_of_realities</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Teen And Up Audiences</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora/Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora &amp; Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Glimmer (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Shadow Weaver | Light Spinner (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Hordak (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Horde Prime (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Bow (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Melog (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Character Study</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Angst</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Implied/Referenced Child Abuse</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Past Child Abuse</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Shadow Weaver | Light Spinner (She-Ra)'s A+ Parenting</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Implied/Referenced Torture</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Abandonment Issues</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>implied suicidal ideation</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Redemption</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Healing</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Trauma</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Hurt No Comfort</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>at least for the first chapter</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>she gets to start healing come the second chapter I promise</rdf:li>
